    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "REA Dooley Group are delighted to present this substantial detached bungalow, ideally positioned on the ever-popular Smiths Road, just a few minutes` drive from Charleville town centre.\n\nSet on a private, enclosed site and extending to approximately 120 sq. m., this well-proportioned property offers excellent potential as a comfortable family home or an ideal option for those looking to downsize while retaining generous living and outdoor space.\n\nThe accommodation begins with a sliding-door entrance into a welcoming porch, leading through to the hallway with carpet flooring. The spacious sitting room is located just off the hallway and features an open fireplace, carpet flooring and built-in shelving/units to one alcove.\n\nThe adjoining dining room enjoys a warm and inviting feel, with timber flooring, an open fireplace and views over the rear garden. The generously proportioned kitchen is fitted with pine-style units and tiled flooring, with a solid-fuel stove with back boiler set within an attractive feature stone fireplace. A useful adjoining storage area provides plumbing for laundry appliances and access to the rear garden. Also off the kitchen is a versatile additional room, which serves as a forth bedroom or home office complete with a timber floor and built-in unit. \n\nThe bedrooms are generously sized, each benefiting from extensive built-in wardrobes. Two bedrooms are further enhanced by en-suite shower rooms, both fully tiled and fitted with electric showers. The main family bathroom is also fully tiled and features a bath tub.\n\nExternally, the property is approached through a walled and gated entrance, complemented by black wrought-iron railings and a tarmac driveway providing ample off-street parking. Mature lawns extend to the side and rear, with established hedging providing an excellent degree of privacy. An attached garage with front roller door offers valuable additional storage or parking, while a garden shed is positioned towards the end of the garden.\n\nThe location is a key feature of this property. Within easy walking distance of Charleville town centre, residents can enjoy convenient access to a wide range of amenities including schools, supermarkets, cafs, restaurants and public transport. Charleville is also ideally situated on the N20, providing excellent connectivity to both Cork and Limerick.\n\nThis is an excellent opportunity to acquire a spacious detached bungalow in a highly sought-after and convenient location, offering a combination of generous accommodation, established gardens, privacy and considerable potential.\n\nViewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate all this property has to offer.\n\nEntrance Porch\n3.52m x 1.13m Entrance via sliding door to porch, tiled floor, timber panelling\n\nHallway\n4.19m x 1.29m Carpet, radiator\n\nCorridor\n4.30m x 1.09m Carpet, stira stairs to attic\n\nSitting Room\n4.00m x 3.93m Open fireplace, built-in units, carpet, power points, TV point, radiator\n\nDining Room\n3.70m x 3.40m Open fireplace, timber floor, radiator, power points\n\nKitchen\n5.85m x 3.42m Built-in Pine units, tiled floor, solid fuel stove with back boiler, power points, tiled splash back\n\nStorage Area\n1.60m x 0.85 Fully plumbed, radiator, tiled floor, tiled wall to wall, access to rear\n\nBedroom/Office\n2.83m x 2.42m Timber floor, built-in wardrobe, power points, radiator\n\nBedroom\n2.79m x 2.55 Carpet, built-in wardrobes, radiator, power points\n\nBedroom\n4.12m x 3.98m Carpet, built-in wardrobes, radiator, power points\n\nEn-Suite\n2.32 m x 1.80m Tiled floor, tiled wall to wall, extractor, WC, WHB, electric shower\n\nBedroom\n3.72m x 3.02m Carpet, radiator, power points\n\nEn-Suite\n2.30m x 1.80m Tiled floor, tiled wall to wall, extractor, WC, WHB, electric shower\n\nBathroom\n2.43m x 1.85m Tiled floor, tiled wall to wall, radiator, WC, WHB, bath, shaving light, bath\n\nAttached Garage\n7.40m x 3.63m Roller door, power points, light\n\nGarden shed\n10.02m x 4.3m\n\n\nDirections\nP56 HR82\n\nNotice\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only."
